WEBVTT

00:00:00.200 --> 00:00:05.014
First find the unit rate or scaling factor, then apply that factor consistently to

00:00:05.014 --> 00:00:06.045
the new situation.

00:00:06.867 --> 00:00:12.960
At a fixed rate of 5 items per 3 people, find the items for 9 people. The answer is

00:00:12.960 --> 00:00:16.808
15. Both parts scale by 3, so 5 times 3 equals 15.

00:00:17.617 --> 00:00:22.994
A class at a science exhibition uses 3 bottles for 3 pupils. At the same rate, how

00:00:22.994 --> 00:00:26.790
many bottles are needed for 6 pupils? Pause to choose and explain.

00:00:27.617 --> 00:00:33.038
A class at a science exhibition uses 3 bottles for 3 pupils. At the same rate, how

00:00:33.038 --> 00:00:38.778
many bottles are needed for 6 pupils? The answer is 6. Both parts scale by 2, so 3

00:00:38.778 --> 00:00:40.054
times 2 equals 6.
